<section class="gg-support-board-hero">
  <div class="gg-support-board-bg"></div>

  <div class="gg-container gg-support-board-grid">
    <div class="gg-support-board-copy reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker">Support Goal Grower</span>

      <h1>Help turn a beta into something people can return to.</h1>

      <p>
        Goal Grower is being built to make progress feel visual, human, and alive.
        Support helps with testing, design polish, launch prep, and future features.
      </p>

      <div class="gg-hero-actions">
        <a href="/collections/all" class="gg-btn">Support the Project</a>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="gg-btn-soft">Become a Tester</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-support-board-visual reveal">
      <div class="gg-board-card board-main">
        <span>Current stage</span>
        <strong>Beta</strong>
        <p>Goal tracking, personal gardens, and shared gardens are being tested now.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-board-card board-small board-testing">
        <span>Testing</span>
        <strong>Real devices</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-board-card board-small board-polish">
        <span>Design</span>
        <strong>More clarity</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-board-card board-small board-launch">
        <span>Launch</span>
        <strong>App store prep</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-support-letter">
  <div class="gg-container gg-support-letter-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker">Why this matters</span>
      <h2>This is not just another productivity app.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-support-letter-text reveal">
      <p>
        Most productivity tools make progress feel like performance. Goal Grower is different:
        it turns goals into something you care for, return to, and slowly build over time.
      </p>

      <p>
        Support helps the app become more stable, more beautiful, and more useful for
        real people with real goals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-support-map">
  <div class="gg-container">
    <div class="gg-section-heading reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker">Where support goes</span>
      <h2>A simple map of what moves forward.</h2>
      <p>
        Each kind of support helps a different part of the project grow.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-map-layout">
      <div class="gg-map-center reveal">
        <span>Goal Grower</span>
        <strong>Launch Path</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-map-item map-one reveal">
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Testing</h3>
        <p>Real users help find bugs, confusing flows, and rough edges.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-map-item map-two reveal">
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Design polish</h3>
        <p>Support helps make the app calmer, clearer, and easier to use.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-map-item map-three reveal">
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Launch prep</h3>
        <p>Screenshots, store copy, review requirements, and release materials.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gg-map-item map-four reveal">
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Future features</h3>
        <p>Shared gardens, reminders, widgets, and deeper goal systems.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-support-roles">
  <div class="gg-container">
    <div class="gg-section-heading reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker">Choose your role</span>
      <h2>There is more than one way to help.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-role-lanes">
      <a href="/pages/contact" class="gg-role-lane reveal">
        <span>Tester</span>
        <h3>Use the beta.</h3>
        <p>Try the current app and share what feels useful, confusing, or motivating.</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/collections/all" class="gg-role-lane featured reveal">
        <span>Supporter</span>
        <h3>Fund the build.</h3>
        <p>Help cover development, testing, design, and release preparation.</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/collections/all" class="gg-role-lane reveal">
        <span>Customer</span>
        <h3>Shop the mission.</h3>
        <p>Support through digital tools, products, and future Goal Grower items.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-support-now">
  <div class="gg-container gg-support-now-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker light">Right now</span>
      <h2>The next version needs real feedback.</h2>
      <p>
        The app already has the beginning of the experience: goal tracking, garden views,
        goal details, and shared gardens. The next step is learning what real users need.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-now-list reveal">
      <div>
        <strong>What makes people return?</strong>
        <span>Testing reveals what feels motivating.</span>
      </div>

      <div>
        <strong>Where do users get stuck?</strong>
        <span>Feedback helps remove friction before launch.</span>
      </div>

      <div>
        <strong>What should grow next?</strong>
        <span>Support helps decide what features matter most.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-support-close">
  <div class="gg-container">
    <div class="gg-support-close-panel reveal">
      <span class="gg-kicker">Thank you</span>

      <h2>Help build something intentional.</h2>

      <p>
        If Goal Grower feels like something that should exist, you can help bring it
        closer to release by testing, supporting, or sharing the project.
      </p>

      <div class="gg-hero-actions center">
        <a href="/collections/all" class="gg-btn">Support Now</a>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="gg-btn-soft">Join Testing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Goal Grower Support",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Goal Grower Support"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}